<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shota Rustaveli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 12th–early 13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shota Rustaveli was a Georgian poet of the late 12th and early 13th centuries, author of the epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-knight-in-the-panthers-skin">The Knight in the Panther's Skin</a>. He is thought to have served at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a>, possibly as treasurer, and tradition says he ended his life at the Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monastery-of-the-cross">Monastery of the Cross</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, where a fresco portrait of him survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shota-rustaveli.jpg" alt="Shota Rustaveli" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DerFuchs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shota_Rustaveli_fresco_in_the_Monastery_of_the_Cross_in_Jerusalem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
